  "deck": "Alysson's 13 points led a Bin XI that scored 78, more than any side in the league.",
  "body": "Alysson hauled in Aston Villa's 4-4 draw away to Manchester United: a goal and two assists in 70 minutes, two of his three shots on target, and two interceptions besides. Leon Goretzka scored in the same eight-goal match and sits in the middle behind him.\n\nThe back of the side belongs to Sunderland, whose 1-0 win over Chelsea gave Robin Roefs, Trai Hume and Reinildo a clean sheet and carried it into the middle through Noah Sadiki and Luke O'Nien. Roefs was dropped by Bayern Bru ahead of gameweek 8. Nico Elvedi and Costinha kept clean sheets for Leeds United and Brighton & Hove Albion. Nottingham Forest's 3-1 win over Manchester City supplied a goal from Jair Cunha in defence and an assist from Xaver Schlager in midfield. Alysson leads the line alone.",
